# request: "Architecture diagram of our shop platform for the README. Web and mobile
#  clients call a Kong API gateway, which routes REST calls to the Catalog, Orders and
#  Payments services. Catalog and Orders use the Postgres shop DB. Orders publishes
#  order events to Kafka; the Notifications worker consumes them and emails
#  customers through SendGrid. Payments charges cards with Stripe. Highlight Orders."
type: architecture
reader: GitHub README
width: 800
direction: down
focus: services.orders
out: admin UI, observability, CI/CD
nodes:
  web: Web app\nReact
  mobile: Mobile app\niOS, Android
  gateway: API gateway\nKong
  services: Services
  services.catalog: Catalog\nGo
  services.orders: Orders\nJava
  services.notify: Notifications\nPython
  services.payments: Payments\nNode.js
  data: Data
  data.db: Shop DB\nPostgres {shape: cylinder}
  data.events: Events\nKafka {shape: queue}
  saas: Third party
  saas.sendgrid: SendGrid {external}
  saas.stripe: Stripe {external}
edges:
  web -> gateway
  mobile -> gateway
  gateway -> services.orders: REST
  gateway -> services.catalog: REST
  gateway -> services.payments: REST
  services.orders -> data.db
  services.catalog -> data.db
  services.orders -> data.events {dashed}
  data.events -> services.notify {dashed}
  services.notify -> saas.sendgrid
  services.payments -> saas.stripe
